      "sinAstros": true,
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "El Cuervo siguió volando, hasta llegar a gente que pescaba a oscuras, junto a un río.",
          "en": "Raven flew on, until he came to people fishing in the dark, by a river."
        },
        {
          "es": "Les pidió que lo cruzaran, pero no quisieron.",
          "en": "He asked them to take him across, but they would not."
        },
        {
          "es": "'Si no lo hacen', dijo el Cuervo, '¡les suelto la luz del día!' Pero ellos solo discutieron con él.",
          "en": "'If you don't,' said Raven, 'I will let daylight break on you!' But they only argued with him."
        },
        {
          "es": "Entonces el Cuervo abrió la caja. El sol voló al cielo, y hubo luz del día por todas partes.",
          "en": "So Raven opened the box. The sun flew up into the sky, and there was daylight everywhere."
        },
        {
          "es": "Algunos se asustaron tanto que corrieron al mar o al bosque, y se volvieron los animales cuyas pieles llevaban.",
          "en": "Some people were so frightened, they ran into the sea or the forest, and became the animals whose skins they wore."
        }
      ],
